L12: # JSON-RPC error codes
L13: _CODE_METHOD_NOT_FOUND = -32601  # Skill/module not found
L14: _CODE_INVALID_PARAMS = -32602  # Schema validation / invalid input
L15: _CODE_INTERNAL_ERROR = -32603  # Internal / timeout / safety errors
L16: _CODE_TASK_NOT_FOUND = -32001  # Unknown task id, or a task owned by another principal
L17: # Governance refusal codes (srs FR-ERR-003 / FR-ERR-009 / FR-ERR-010).
L18: #
L19: # A2A 1.0 reserves -32001..-32009; JSON-RPC 2.0 leaves -32000..-32099 to the
L20: # implementation. These three sit above A2A's reserved block, with room for it
L21: # to grow, and are the "JSON-RPC custom error" A2A §13.2 names as the example
L22: # for this binding.
L23: #
L24: # apcore distinguishes these three refusals from each other and from every other
L25: # failure. Collapsing them onto -32001 (which means "unknown or non-owned task
L26: # id") or -32603 (which every agent reads as "retry me") told the caller a
L27: # *different* failure had happened, one whose correct response is the opposite
L28: # of the real one.
